WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.730
Two countries.

2
00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:05.290
Niger has 27.0 million people.

3
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.650
Japan has 123.8 million.

4
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.470
Life expectancy at birth
is 84.9 years in Japan,

5
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.950
and 61.4 years in Niger.

6
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.270
Yet at today's rate, Niger's population
would double in roughly 21 years.

7
00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.150
Japan's is shrinking.

8
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.310
Are migrants pouring into Niger?

9
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.390
Is Japan's death rate extremely high?

10
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.190
Or is something else going on?

11
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.670
In this mission, you'll calculate natural
increase from birth and death rates,

12
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.490
and place both countries on the
demographic transition model.

13
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:41.490
Then you'll read population
pyramids, work out dependency ratios,

14
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.690
and test the rule of 70.

15
00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:48.370
Your mission: explain why Niger's
population is set to grow so fast,

16
00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.290
while Japan's shrinks.
